\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Radio safety at the certificate boundary on two nodes. (a) End of the last recovery in every attempt of the bound-padded boundary diagnostic. E4 offers a 256-token unit with two required recoveries at 45\nonbreakingspace ms; E6b and E6a offer a 64-token unit with one required recovery at 89 and 88\nonbreakingspace ms. Baseline attempts launch the unit anyway: idle-time admission in E4 and a shadow launch of the unit that SoftWall\xspace  rejects in E6b. (b) AI units per prompt length in the two-node campaign: units that SoftWall\xspace  runs and units that it rejects because they break the certified recovery bound; idle-time admission would run all of them, and static reservation runs none.}}{18}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval-safety}{{13}{18}{Radio safety at the certificate boundary on two nodes. (a) End of the last recovery in every attempt of the bound-padded boundary diagnostic. E4 offers a 256-token unit with two required recoveries at 45~ms; E6b and E6a offer a 64-token unit with one required recovery at 89 and 88~ms. Baseline attempts launch the unit anyway: idle-time admission in E4 and a shadow launch of the unit that \sys rejects in E6b. (b) AI units per prompt length in the two-node campaign: units that \sys runs and units that it rejects because they break the certified recovery bound; idle-time admission would run all of them, and static reservation runs none}{figure.caption.19}{}}
