\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Execution refinement and radio commit time. (a) Arrival of each AI lease at the Qwen worker relative to its absolute latest-start: the 1,077 leases of the two-node campaign and the 52 leases that the held-lease fault keeps past the latest-start. (b) Commit time of every recovered TB in the two-node campaign, grouped by the prompt length of the AI lease that runs before its recovery; the dotted line marks the median commit of the TBs that NeuralRx\xspace  decodes. (c) Commit time of every TB under each injected fault: no fault, all TBs of a period fail, stale and duplicate NeuralRx\xspace  outcomes, a late AI reply after GPU completion, an AI lease held past its latest-start, an AI channel lost before GPU completion, and stale and duplicate recovery responses.}}{19}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eval-refinement}{{14}{19}{Execution refinement and radio commit time. (a) Arrival of each AI lease at the Qwen worker relative to its absolute latest-start: the 1,077 leases of the two-node campaign and the 52 leases that the held-lease fault keeps past the latest-start. (b) Commit time of every recovered TB in the two-node campaign, grouped by the prompt length of the AI lease that runs before its recovery; the dotted line marks the median commit of the TBs that \NRx decodes. (c) Commit time of every TB under each injected fault: no fault, all TBs of a period fail, stale and duplicate \NRx outcomes, a late AI reply after GPU completion, an AI lease held past its latest-start, an AI channel lost before GPU completion, and stale and duplicate recovery responses}{figure.caption.20}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Predictive scheduling and control cost. (a) Latest decision time at which one AI unit of each prompt length remains admissible with four admitted TBs and zero to four pending recoveries; circles and crosses mark the prespecified physical tests that the scheduler admitted and rejected, labeled with their prompt length. (b) Candidate construction and independent verification latency against the number of pending recoveries, with the evaluated 5\nonbreakingspace ms control budget. Latencies are finite-run measurements, not WCETs.}}{20}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:envelope}{{15}{20}{Predictive scheduling and control cost. (a) Latest decision time at which one AI unit of each prompt length remains admissible with four admitted TBs and zero to four pending recoveries; circles and crosses mark the prespecified physical tests that the scheduler admitted and rejected, labeled with their prompt length. (b) Candidate construction and independent verification latency against the number of pending recoveries, with the evaluated 5~ms control budget. Latencies are finite-run measurements, not WCETs}{figure.caption.21}{}}
